20260529.115826.521 [<kpop..........] I added a failing regression test that compares `posterior()` against rev `9eaa27`.
20260529.115826.713 [<kpop..........] ## What I found
20260529.115827.202 [<kpop..........] At `9eaa27`, `get_neighbor_data` called `model.index().search()` (FAISS) directly. HEAD routes through `index_search` →
20260529.115827.733 [<kpop..........] `exact_f64_batch_topk`, which adds neighbor-phase overhead on top of the stats work. That shows up as `posterior_median /
20260529.115828.356 [<kpop..........] faiss_neighbor_median` well above the small ratio `9eaa27` had, for both `tie_break_neighbors` settings:
20260529.115828.413 [<kpop..........] | n | tie_break | ratio (HEAD) |
20260529.115828.569 [<kpop..........] |---|-----------|--------------|
20260529.115828.815 [<kpop..........] | 512 | off/on | ~1.34 / ~1.43 |
20260529.115829.062 [<kpop..........] | 1024 | off/on | ~1.19 / ~1.24 |
20260529.115829.249 [<kpop..........] ## What I added
20260529.115829.832 [<kpop..........] 1. **`tests/fixtures/posterior_speed_baseline.json`** — baseline from rev `9eaa27`; caps `posterior/faiss` at **1.12×** (ref
20260529.115830.241 [<kpop..........] **1.08×** for FAISS + stats) for n=512 and n=1024 self-search.
20260529.115830.705 [<kpop..........] 2. **`test_posterior_self_search_not_slower_than_9eaa27_baseline`** in `tests/test_enn_perf.py` — parametrized over
20260529.115830.996 [<kpop..........] `tie_break_neighbors ∈ {False, True}`; fails on current code:
20260529.115831.044 [<kpop..........] ```text
20260529.115831.543 [<kpop..........] random_self_search_512 tie_break=True: posterior/faiss=1.431x exceeds 9eaa27 cap 1.12x
20260529.115831.561 [<kpop..........] ```
20260529.115831.682 [<kpop..........] Run it with:
20260529.115831.753 [<kpop..........] ```bash
20260529.115832.142 [<kpop..........] PYTHONPATH=src pytest -sv tests/test_enn_perf.py::test_posterior_self_search_not_slower_than_9eaa27_baseline
20260529.115832.161 [<kpop..........] ```
20260529.115832.771 [<kpop..........] **Executive summary:** The test treats FAISS-only neighbor lookup as the `9eaa27` neighbor path and asserts
20260529.115833.397 [<kpop..........] `posterior(train_x)` stays within 12% of that. HEAD is ~19–43% over budget at n=512/1024, independent of tie_break.
20260529.115834.019 [<kpop..........] **tl;dr:** New perf test fails because `posterior` is ~1.2–1.4× slower than the FAISS neighbor baseline from rev `9eaa27`,
20260529.115834.219 [<kpop..........] for both tie_break settings.
